sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-10> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-10--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-10--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch16-10: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.56" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.564"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.57"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Spine height is directly measurable on open CT once a bending-moment model is specified. That model is the cantilever picture of the preceding claim, so errors in mass distribution carry into the regression. A comparative sample can test proportionality in well-studied species and will confound mechanical moment with muscle attachment area." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Measure neural-spine height at each vertebra and regress it on the bending moment predicted from body-segment masses and the positions of the limb supports. A positive proportional fit would support the claim; spine height that follows muscle size or display with no relation to the moment diagram would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Segment masses and support points are only partly available in the same files as the skeletons.", "Tall spines also anchor ligaments and epaxial muscles and, in some species, display structures." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch16-10--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch16-10--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-10--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch16-10 by Grok 4.7: 0.72" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.72"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-10--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-10> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-10--grok--operationalizability> .
